well this is a reflection about seeing  the Earth from space it's a kind of  meditation on what transpires within our  very Consciousness as we gaze upon the  pale blue dot these words are by Dom  delillo and I find them so  poignant  here goes  the view is endlessly fulfilling it is  like the answer to a lifetime of  questions and vague Cravings it  satisfies every childlike curiosity  every muted desire whatever there is in  him of the scientist the poet  primitive Seer The Watcher of fire and  shooting stars whatever obsessions eat  at the night side of his mind whatever  sweet and dreamy yearning he has ever  felt for nameless places far away  whatever Earth Sense he possesses the  neural pulse of some Wilder awareness  sympathy for beasts whatever belief in  an imminent vital force the Lord of  creation whatever secret harboring of  the idea of human Oneness whatever  wishfulness and simple-hearted hope  whatever of too much and not enough all  at once and little by little whatever  burning urge to escape responsibility  and routine Escape his own over  specialization the circumscribed and  inward spiraling self whatever remnants  of his boyish Longing To Fly his dreams  of strange spaces and Eerie Heights  fantasies of happy death whatever  indolent and sybaritic leanings Lotus  eater smoker of grasses and herbs  blue-eyed gazer into space  all of these are satisfied all collected  and masked in that living body the sight  he sees  in that window  now I don't know about you but I feel  transported by these words and they  really do seem like the answer to the  existential question to the weight of  being to the question of what to do with  ourselves  the answer it seems simply to Marvel  [Music]
 

